 {"version_id": "prompt-19", "phase": "prompt", "technique": "Evidence-traced call-chain localization", "target_failure_mode": "Complex repository-specific diagnosis and implementation", "expected_dimension": "reasoning_soundness", "evidence_instance_ids": ["scikit-learn__scikit-learn-15100", "pytest-dev__pytest-7432", "django__django-16938", "astropy__astropy-13033"], "patch_or_prompt": {"file": "trae_agent/agent/trae_agent.py", "find": "Before editing a framework or scientific-library change, perform evidence-gated repository localization: first write a short hypothesis about the failure, then verify it by tracing the reported input through the concrete call chain to the failing output.", "replace": "Before editing a framework or scientific-library change, perform evidence-gated repository localization: state the reported input, expected output, observed output, and a falsifiable hypothesis; then trace that exact input through the concrete call chain, including normalization, dispatch, state mutation, and output construction, until you identify the first point where behavior diverges."}, "dimensions": {"target_alignment": 0.92, "reasoning_soundness": 0.89, "execution_accuracy": 0.84, "output_integrity": 0.88}, "aggregate": 0.8825, "probe_scores": [{"instance_id": "scikit-learn__scikit-learn-15100", "score": 0.96}, {"instance_id": "pytest-dev__pytest-7432", "score": 0.96}, {"instance_id": "django__django-16938", "score": 0.35}, {"instance_id": "astropy__astropy-13033", "score": 0.3}], "score_label": "PROXY", "decision": "applied", "apply_note": "applied+committed", "delta_vs_baseline": 0.0475, "why": "Evidence-gated call-chain tracing directly addresses repository-specific diagnosis and reduces speculative edits, producing the strongest improvement on the complex Django and Astropy cases. The required localization overhead limits execution gains slightly."}
 {"version_id": "prompt-20", "phase": "prompt", "technique": "Change-surface and contract inventory", "target_failure_mode": "Complex repository-specific diagnosis and implementation", "expected_dimension": "target_alignment", "evidence_instance_ids": ["scikit-learn__scikit-learn-15100", "pytest-dev__pytest-7432", "django__django-16938", "astropy__astropy-13033"], "patch_or_prompt": {"file": "trae_agent/agent/trae_agent.py", "find": "Identify the primary implementation and construct a change-surface map covering every relevant caller, subclass or override, alternate backend, serializer/parser, configuration default, public API boundary, and existing regression test.", "replace": "Identify the primary implementation and construct a change-surface map before editing: list every relevant caller, subclass or override, alternate backend, serializer/parser, configuration default, public API boundary, and existing regression test, and for each record the current contract, whether it should change, and why the proposed edit will not unintentionally alter unrelated paths."}, "dimensions": {"target_alignment": 0.89, "reasoning_soundness": 0.87, "execution_accuracy": 0.81, "output_integrity": 0.88}, "aggregate": 0.8625, "probe_scores": [{"instance_id": "scikit-learn__scikit-learn-15100", "score": 0.95}, {"instance_id": "pytest-dev__pytest-7432", "score": 0.95}, {"instance_id": "django__django-16938", "score": 0.29}, {"instance_id": "astropy__astropy-13033", "score": 0.25}], "score_label": "PROXY", "decision": "applied", "apply_note": "applied+committed", "delta_vs_baseline": 0.0275, "why": "A contract and change-surface inventory improves awareness of callers and alternate implementations, but it is more static and potentially overbroad than direct call-chain localization. It helps complex cases modestly while adding planning cost and no strong validation mechanism."}
 {"version_id": "prompt-21", "phase": "prompt", "technique": "Failure-directed validation loop", "target_failure_mode": "Insufficient validation and iterative debugging", "expected_dimension": "execution_accuracy", "evidence_instance_ids": ["scikit-learn__scikit-learn-15100", "pytest-dev__pytest-7432", "django__django-16938", "astropy__astropy-13033"], "patch_or_prompt": {"file": "trae_agent/agent/trae_agent.py", "find": "After implementing the change, validate it with the narrowest relevant regression test, then run broader targeted tests and inspect failures rather than assuming the first patch is complete.", "replace": "After implementing the change, run a tight validation loop: execute the smallest reproducer or focused regression test, inspect the complete failure and traceback, classify it as implementation, test-assumption, environment, or unrelated failure, revise the hypothesis and patch when needed, rerun the focused test, and only then expand to related module tests and the broader suite."}, "dimensions": {"target_alignment": 0.86, "reasoning_soundness": 0.85, "execution_accuracy": 0.88, "output_integrity": 0.88}, "aggregate": 0.8675, "probe_scores": [{"instance_id": "scikit-learn__scikit-learn-15100", "score": 0.97}, {"instance_id": "pytest-dev__pytest-7432", "score": 0.97}, {"instance_id": "django__django-16938", "score": 0.32}, {"instance_id": "astropy__astropy-13033", "score": 0.29}], "score_label": "PROXY", "decision": "proposed_not_applied", "apply_note": "find-block matched 0x (need exactly 1)", "delta_vs_baseline": 0.0325, "why": "The tight reproducer, traceback classification, and rerun loop directly improve validation and iterative debugging, giving the largest execution-accuracy gain. It does not substantially improve initial repository diagnosis, so complex cases remain weaker than with localization-focused changes."}
